From 9ec770ee1871ffe64dc52fc9f95531882029ba45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:27:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/34] usb_webcam: decode MJPEG from UVC cameras

Uncompressed video over USB 2.0 is slow at large sizes: the C920
sends 1920x1080 at 5 fps as YUY2, but at 30 fps as MJPEG.

UVCCamDevice now keeps the uncompressed and the MJPEG format, offers
the sizes of both through UVCFrameList, probes with the format and
frame index of the chosen size and decodes each frame by its format.
Format and frame descriptors are only read as far as they are long,
and the BLists of frame descriptors, which were never freed, are
gone. A start fails if the decoder got no memory.

VideoSizeAt() returns a cam_video_size, and the size label names the
format: "1920 x 1080 (30 fps, MJPEG)".

With a Logitech C920 (046d:08e5) on a ThinkPad T470s, 1920x1080 now
runs at 29.8 fps instead of 5; decoding takes a quarter of one core.

Signed-off-by: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
(cherry picked from commit 6b09bb43eebf284aa2b41dd4982f23dfad9042c4)
